WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.919
Right into audience questions for the week.

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:07.730
First one is, Hey David, I get Michael Bloomberg
is doing okay in the polls, but what's the

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.980
point of him campaigning for the presidency?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:10.980
He can't win.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.980
He's [inaudible],

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:12.980
he's nearly 80 years old.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.339
He's merely hemorrhaging cash.

00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:16.420
What is the point of this entire thing?

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.789
So I think there's a couple of different things
going on.

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:25.550
Number one, the spending of the money, so
given that Michael Bloomberg is running for

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.650
him, the spending of the money, he probably
sees as a better and more efficient way to

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:36.570
get his message directly to voters than participation
in the debates after having an individual

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.850
donation infrastructure.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.510
So he's chosen to forego individual donations.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.190
He spending a whole bunch of money, it could
be 150 million by now, could could be even

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.190
more.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:48.789
I don't know that we have the latest tally
and he believes that he has a good message

00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:53.629
and he is choosing to go directly to voters
and that explains the spending of the money.

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:58.760
If you have 55 billion spending 100 million
or 200 million or 300 million, these are unconscionable

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.960
amounts of money for 99.99% of the population
or or more.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.400
But to Michael Bloomberg, it's really, it's
barely anything, particularly when he's nearly

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.950
80 years old and he has all the money and
his kids, I don't know anything about his

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.560
family, but his kids, I'm sure I have all
the money they could ever need, so the spending

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.850
of the money, you have to think about it as
like spending pennies and that's effectively

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.230
what he is doing.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:28.400
Secondly, I think the strategy of running
at all, because again, if the thing doesn't

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.030
change drastically, he is obviously not going
to be the nominee.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:39.579
There is a gamble that Biden fails and people
get scared of voting Bernie or voting Warren

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:44.680
and Bloomberg is there with name recognition
and having built up a campaign infrastructure

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:48.920
as well as just blasting out hundreds of millions
of dollars in ads.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:55.310
Now it may not work because the the obvious
alternative to an establishment Democrat like

00:01:55.310 --> 00:02:01.360
Biden is not to go to the guy who got in late,
hasn't been in any of the debates and was

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.550
a Republican for a long time in his life.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:08.450
I think they go to boot edge edge or they
go to Amy Klobuchar to fill the establishment

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:11.160
role if were to totally falter.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:16.800
I do believe that underlying all of this,
I believe Michael Bloomberg is sincere, that

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.750
he wants to remove Donald Trump at all costs
and there was the concern of, well Bloomberg's

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:25.720
in there because he's super rich and he wants
to protect his own wealth.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:31.570
There's probably ways in which that's true,
but he may also be wanting to protect merely

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:36.530
the structures that allow him to make money
rather than avoiding a wealth tax.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.480
Personally, because I read over the weekend
that he said he would support whoever the

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.930
democratic nominee ultimately is, including
Elizabeth Warren, whose wealth tax would directly

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.500
affect Michael Bloomberg, and I'm sure he
doesn't believe that her wealth tax will become

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.480
a reality and that's probably a good assessment.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.420
He says he would vote for Bernie, so on and
so forth.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:56.230
So I don't want another billionaire president.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:00.140
I've not seen evidence that Michael Bloomberg
is acting in bad faith.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:05.150
And of course it's F w what his candidacy
really is, is not evidence of a guy acting

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.610
in bad faith.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:11.950
It's just evidence of why the money and politics
system that we have is so corrosive because

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:17.530
he switched from being a Republican to a Democrat
during Donald Trump's tenure, bought his way

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:21.920
in without being in a single debate and his
polling at last check, something like five

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:22.990
or 6%.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:27.880
I don't think he's a bad faith actor, but
he does show us why the system we have doesn't

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.780
work and why it should be very quickly changed.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:36.190
I a also, by the way, I would love to get
a phone call when we do live calls from a

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.360
Michael Bloomberg supporter.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.700
I jokingly tweeted over the weekend that I,
I, I met a real Amy Klobuchar supporter in

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:48.560
real life and I, I in, in person, I don't
think I know anyone who's supporting Clover

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.340
char or Biden.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:53.610
I know a couple people I'm friends with on
Facebook who are supporting mayor Pete.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.800
Um, I don't, I've not talked to anyone who
is supporting Michael Bloomberg and I would

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.340
love to get a call from them during live calls
next week.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.580
So if you're supporting Bloomberg, I want
to hear from you.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.670
Is it issue oriented?

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:08.790
Is it personality, is it you want a billionaire
to face off against Trump or what exactly

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.690
is it that you see as appealing about Michael
Bloomberg?

